# Agent git worktrees. These are full checkouts of this repository living
# INSIDE it, created by concurrent sessions. Untracked, they are one
# `git add -A` away from being committed three times over; and Prettier
# walked into them and reported every task file as unformatted, which is
# how they were noticed.
.claude/worktrees/

# YT-0424: Serwist's generated service worker bundle (apps/web/app/sw.ts is
# the real source). Built output, same as `.next/` above — not committed,
# and staying out of source control means a stale bundle from one bundler
# flavour (see this ticket's report: `next build`'s default Turbopack never
# emits this file at all; only `next build --webpack` does) can never be
# mistaken for a fresh one.
#
# Narrowed to the one file: `apps/web/public/` is Next.js's conventional
# static-asset directory, so ignoring it wholesale would mean a favicon,
# manifest or image added later is silently never committed.
#
# This file also PERSISTS across builds -- `next build` clears `.next/`,
# not `public/`. A Turbopack build leaves the previous webpack build's
# bundle in place, so a service worker can be served that no longer
# matches `sw.ts`. `playwright.offline.config.ts` is safe because it
# rebuilds with `--webpack` every run; anything else reading it should
# delete it first rather than trust that it is current.
apps/web/public/sw.js

# scripts/progress.mjs holds this while it rewrites TASKS.md
TASKS.md.lock
# Per-machine Claude Code permissions; every track worktree writes one (TASKS.md session protocol)
.claude/settings.local.json
# Third-party clips fetched for the design prototypes (TASKS.md 3.2.a); licences in CREDITS.txt
apps/web/public/lab-media/
